    <forecast>
        <area aac="SA_FA001" description="South Australia" type="region">
            <forecast-period start-time-local="2026-11-12T10:53:24+10:30" end-time-local="2026-11-12T10:53:24+10:30" start-time-utc="2026-11-12T00:23:24Z" end-time-utc="2026-11-12T00:23:24Z">
                <text type="warning_summary_footer">For latest warnings go to www.bom.gov.au, subscribe to RSS feeds, call 1300 659 210* or listen for warnings on relevant TV and radio broadcasts.</text>
                <text type="synoptic_situation">A ridge of high pressure lies over water south of the Bight and will weaken this evening. A low pressure system over Western Australian will move over South Australia on Friday, with an associated trough. A ridge of high pressure will follow and persist into early next week. A cold front clips the southeast on Sunday.</text>
                <text type="product_footer">* Calls to 1300 numbers cost around 27.5c incl. GST, higher from mobiles or public phones.</text>
            </forecast-period>
        </area>
        <area aac="SA_PW014" description="North East Pastoral" type="public-district" parent-aac="SA_FA001">
            <forecast-period index="0" start-time-local="2026-11-12T00:00:00+10:30" end-time-local="2026-11-13T00:00:00+10:30" start-time-utc="2026-11-11T13:30:00Z" end-time-utc="2026-11-12T13:30:00Z">
                <text type="forecast">Partly cloudy. Medium chance of showers west of Leigh Creek, slight chance elsewhere. The chance of a thunderstorm north of Leigh Creek in the late afternoon and evening. Winds northeast to southeasterly 15 to 25 km/h tending northwest to southwesterly in the early afternoon then tending southeast to southwesterly in the late afternoon. Daytime maximum temperatures 32 to 40.</text>
                <text type="fire_danger">High</text>
                <text type="uv_alert">Sun protection 9:00am to 5:00pm, UV Index predicted to reach 11 [Extreme]</text>
            </forecast-period>
            <forecast-period index="1" start-time-local="2026-11-13T00:00:00+10:30" end-time-local="2026-11-14T00:00:00+10:30" start-time-utc="2026-11-12T13:30:00Z" end-time-utc="2026-11-13T13:30:00Z">
                <text type="forecast">Partly cloudy. Medium chance of showers, most likely in the morning and early afternoon. The chance of a thunderstorm. Winds northeast to southeasterly 15 to 20 km/h tending northwest to northeasterly 20 to 30 km/h in the morning then tending northwest to southwesterly in the middle of the day. Overnight temperatures falling to between 18 and 25 with daytime temperatures reaching 31 to 38.</text>
            </forecast-period>
            <forecast-period index="2" start-time-local="2026-11-14T00:00:00+10:30" end-time-local="2026-11-15T00:00:00+10:30" start-time-utc="2026-11-13T13:30:00Z" end-time-utc="2026-11-14T13:30:00Z">
                <text type="forecast">Mostly sunny. Slight chance of a shower in the far northeast, near zero chance elsewhere. The chance of a thunderstorm in the morning and afternoon. Winds south to southwesterly 20 to 30 km/h increasing to 25 to 35 km/h during the morning. Overnight temperatures falling to between 16 and 24 with daytime temperatures reaching 30 to 38.</text>
            </forecast-period>
            <forecast-period index="3" start-time-local="2026-11-15T00:00:00+10:30" end-time-local="2026-11-16T00:00:00+10:30" start-time-utc="2026-11-14T13:30:00Z" end-time-utc="2026-11-15T13:30:00Z">
                <text type="forecast">Sunny morning. The chance of a thunderstorm north of Oodnadatta in the afternoon and evening. Winds southerly 25 to 40 km/h. Overnight temperatures falling to between 11 and 23 with daytime temperatures reaching 26 to 35.</text>
            </forecast-period>
        </area>
